  "merger_description": "CAMP Australia Pty Ltd, which is an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of CA Group Holdco Pty Ltd (together, **Camp Australia**), proposes to acquire 20 outside school hours care (**OSHC**) businesses and their associated assets from Jabiru Community Services Limited (**Jabiru**) by way of asset sale (the Acquisition).\n\nCamp Australia is a Victoria-headquartered, national OSHC services provider, delivering before school care, after school care, pupil free day care and vacation care programmes to primary school-aged children in all states and territories. Camp Australia provides services at approximately 442 schools across Australia, including 68 services in Queensland. Camp Australia is owned by a consortium of private investment funds led by Allegro Funds.\n\nJabiru is a not-for-profit organisation headquartered in Bracken Ridge Queensland and provides OSHC programmes to primary-school aged children in South-East Queensland. Jabiru currently provides OSHC services at 22 schools in Queensland, 20 of which are the subject of the Acquisition.\n\nCamp Australia and Jabiru overlap in the supply of OSHC services and vacation care services in Queensland.",
